        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): bound legacy sessions.json reads during SQLite inspect",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nDoctor's legacy `sessions.json` → SQLite inspect/migrate path used unbounded `fs.readFileSync`, so a corrupted or adversarial store could force a large in-memory allocation during `openclaw doctor --session-sqlite`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCap the shared legacy-store reader at 16 MiB with `readRegularFileSync`, matching other doctor/state byte ceilings. That ceiling is an intentional support boundary: valid stores above 16 MiB fail closed as `store_unreadable` instead of partial migrate. Operator messaging and docs spell out the limit and recovery (backup, prune via `openclaw sessions cleanup`, retry).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Oversized legacy `sessions.json` (>16 MiB) no longer loads unbounded during doctor inspect / dry-run / import / validate.\n- Report issue `store_unreadable` names the 16 MiB support limit and next steps.\n- No SQLite create, no archive, no partial migrate for oversized stores.\n- Stores at or under 16 MiB keep the previous migrate path.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Code\n\n- `src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.ts`: `LEGACY_SESSION_STORE_MAX_BYTES = 16 MiB`; `readLegacySessionRecords` uses `readRegularFileSync`; oversized reads get a recovery-focused `store_unreadable` message.\n- `docs/cli/doctor.md`: Session SQLite section notes the legacy store size ceiling and fail-closed behavior.\n\n### Focused tests\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts -t \"legacy sessions.json\" --reporter=verbose\n```\n\nResult (3 passed):\n\n- fail-closes **inspect** when legacy sessions.json exceeds the 16 MiB support limit\n- fail-closes **dry-run** when legacy sessions.json exceeds the 16 MiB support limit\n- fail-closes **import** when legacy sessions.json exceeds the 16 MiB support limit\n\nAssertions: `store_unreadable` with 16 MiB support-limit messaging; `legacyEntries`/`importedEntries` = 0; SQLite path not created; legacy store not archived.\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nDoctor does not migrate oversized stores. Operators must back up, reduce the store (for example `openclaw sessions cleanup`), then retry `openclaw doctor --session-sqlite import`.\n",
